  "baseline_spec": {
    "name": "white-poplar",
    "notes": "THE TWO-TONE CROWN CANNOT BE SAID AT ALL. A white poplar's leaves are dark above and white-felted underneath, so the crown flares silver when wind turns it -- that is a per-FACE colour on a leaf that does not exist at 10 cm, and no material in the palette has two sides. Recorded because it is the species' most quoted feature and it is not in here.\n\nWhat is here is the pale bole and the stand: `bark_pale` with `cluster` 0.9 at 4 m spacing, because a poplar suckers and comes in thickets. That makes it the second clonal tree in the library and it is deliberately NOT `quaking-aspen`: twice the trunk radius, twice the crown, branches ascending rather than fine and drooping, and placed against water where the aspen is not.",
